# 🔑 Level 00 → 01: SSH Connection & Credentials

![SSH](https://img.shields.io/badge/SSH-000000?style=for-the-badge&logo=OpenSSH&logoColor=white)
![Linux](https://img.shields.io/badge/Linux-FCC624?style=for-the-badge&logo=linux&logoColor=black)
![Security](https://img.shields.io/badge/Security-Red?style=for-the-badge&logo=linux-foundation&logoColor=white)

---

## 🎯 Objective
Establish an encrypted remote SSH session to the target infrastructure over a non-standard port and perform initial file inspection to extract the next-level system credential.

---

## ⚙️ Technical Breakdown

| Parameter | Value | DevOps / Security Context |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Host** | `bandit.labs.overthewire.org` | Target edge host endpoint |
| **Port** | `2220` | Bypasses default TCP `22` to mitigate automated port scanning |
| **User / Pass** | `bandit0` / `bandit0` | Initial entry-level low-privilege identity |
| **Artifact** | `./readme` | Target file containing `bandit1` passkey |

---

## 🚀 Execution & Verification

```bash
# 1. Establish SSH connection over custom port 2220
ssh bandit0@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

# 2. Verify current landing directory and inspect file nodes
pwd     # Output: /home/bandit0
ls -la  # Verify node presence and POSIX permissions

# 3. Read target credential directly to stdout
cat readme
